# graphify scope for PyroScan
#
# The graph is a development aid for "what touches this symbol?" questions.
# It is not part of the runtime. Keep it narrow: vendored code and large binary
# assets drown the real signal (server/ is only ~4.3k lines).

# Vendored frontend: Cesium build + node_modules (336 of 461 files at repo root)
spike/web/node_modules/
spike/web/cesium/
spike/web/cesium-unminified/

# Large binary assets: imagery, screenshots, ODM outputs, reference video
spike/data/
spike/ref/
spike/shots/
spike/missions/
spike/inbox/

# Design references and generated charts: not code, not contracts.
# Indexing them costs semantic extraction and adds no call-graph signal.
Docs/references/
Docs/rab_assets/
Docs/_proposal_*.png
simulation/shots/

# Spike tooling is throwaway by design (see spike/README.md verdict)
spike/tools/

# Data/fixture JSON is not code; AST extraction on it yields noise.
benchmarks/results/
spike/web/data/
server/providers/data/
server/providers/fixtures/
simulation/shots/

# Remaining images: dashboard screenshots only, no semantic value here
spike/web/*.png
Docs/*.png

# Generated HTML (payload studio build output) — not source
simulation/pyroscan_payload_studio.html
simulation/src/studio.html

# My own generated proposal drafts: derived from the docs above, would
# duplicate their entities in the graph. Ignoring the .docx SOURCES also
# stops graphify converting them into graphify-out/converted/*.md at scan time.
Docs/proposal_sections_id.md
Docs/Proposal_PyroScan.docx
Docs/RAB_Payload_PyroScan.docx
converted/

# Generated / local state
graphify-out/
.playwright-mcp/
server/cache/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal
server/*.db
.venv/
venv/
*.log
~$*
*.tmp
